{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/783037-totem-ban-and-bane-ideas-needeed","id":783037,"title":"Totem Ban and bane ideas needeed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T13:41:00-08:00","id":783037,"title":"Totem Ban and bane ideas needeed","content":"Hi<br /> My players (mixed mage and werewolf group) want to have a totem that will come out either as strong rank 1 or as weak rank 2 (depends on what the last player puts into the totem points). <br /> Now my problem is that I'm not sure what a good bans/banes could be good (still getting used to 2nd edition bans). <br /> <br /> <br /> The group is 1 rahu spirit hunting werewolf and 1 mage. <br /> The totem is a &quot;shadow wolf&quot;. A spirit that is associated with the wolves that hunt in the darkness of night and thus in the &quot;shadows&quot;. <br /> Influences will probably be in the area of Darkness, hunt.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was<br /> <br /> Ban: &quot;Must hunt once a month staying in the shadows&quot;<br /> Bane: Must be killed by fangs and claws<br /> <br /> Like I said I'm not sure about the bans and banes what could be fitting. Thus would like some feedback there and maybe additional ideas (also how many does such a spirit need each?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:03:46-08:00","id":783069,"title":"","content":"Very small pack, may I suggest adding some NPCs with dots of their own in Totem?<br /> <br /> Anyway, what about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Ban: Must always make the first srtike in a fight against an oblivious target<br /> <br /> Bane: Weapons made from bones and horns from prey animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:07:48-08:00","id":783074,"title":"","content":"That Ban would conflict the packmates, since they have to follow it as well, and they certainly won't be able to strike first against something all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T15:18:35-08:00","id":783080,"title":"","content":"It was very poorly worded, my bad. What I meant was:<br /> <br /> Ban: You must make your first attack agaisnt a foe (a group is considered a single foe as far as the Ban is concerned) from stealth, trying to take them by surprise.<br /> <br /> Basically, it forces you to use stealth attacks as your default aproach. Once the fight started you can do whatever, but you first have to try to catch them with their guard down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T18:27:05-08:00","id":783181,"title":"","content":"I need the same. The pack is composed of 3 werewolves, and some NPC bloodwolves and some humans. In the near future, a human might join the pack. For some strange reason (role playing reasons) involving a supernatural virus, and a psychic trauma, the human player has now access to some supernatural merits tied to the psychic power area. The Totem is a fox. The name is Watchfox the wise. He is a symbol of perception and wisdom. I do not know what would be an appropriate ban / bane.<br /> <br /> Its quite interesting to develop a Totem, but I always have a hard time finding the appropriate ban/bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T18:30:31-08:00","id":783182,"title":"","content":"Watchfox I could see never hunting something without knowing its weakness.<br /> <br /> @Ryu If it's a really weak spirit just having them hunt only at night could be nicely prohibitive without being crippling, especially if your characters have day jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T09:35:12-08:00","id":783482,"title":"","content":"tnx gave me a few ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T20:58:18-08:00","id":788517,"title":"","content":"I could use some suggestions for a spirit of altered states of mind. Think Dionysus/Bacchus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T06:41:06-08:00","id":788716,"title":"","content":"Ban: May only communicate with those in an altered state of consciousness (meaning if you are sober it won't talk to you or even acknowledge your presence except to smack you down if you get agressive)<br /> <br /> Bane: Pure distilled water? I'm a bit at a loss here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T10:12:41-08:00","id":788840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/783037-totem-ban-and-bane-ideas-needeed?p=788716#post788716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ban: May only communicate with those in an altered state of consciousness (meaning if you are sober it won't talk to you or even acknowledge your presence except to smack you down if you get agressive)<br /> <br /> Bane: Pure distilled water? I'm a bit at a loss here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Klatchian Coffee obviously, it makes you knurd. :3<br /> <br /> Maybe Activated Charcoal? I know they use it to treat orally ingested poisons and drug overdoses.<br /> Also, maybe some of the common sobriety tests like reciting the alphabet backwards? That might be too human of a convention though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","user":"solidork","date":". 12-18-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T10:37:02-08:00","id":788853,"title":"","content":"Or maybe a (general) lethal dose of some specific drug or inebriant. If you can figure out a way to work an <i>amount</i> being a bane, I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T11:24:53-08:00","id":788875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/783037-totem-ban-and-bane-ideas-needeed?p=788517#post788517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could use some suggestions for a spirit of altered states of mind. Think Dionysus/Bacchus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Low Ranking Spirit: Ban: The spirit will only speak to someone who has offered it a mind-altering substance.<br /> Middling Rank: To speak with the spirit, one has to indulge in the spirit's choice of mild-altering drug.<br /> High Ranking: The Spirit loses willpower every week that it has not influenced an overdose.<br /> <br /> Bane: The spirit came into being in the abandoned apartment complex, feeding off of essence from the hosts of junkies and drug deals that passed hands there. The city managed to scrape up enough funds to knock down the building and erect a community rehab center focused on education about drug use. The bricks that make up the rehab's walls are the same bricks that cradled the spirit during it's formative time. Weapons made from any brick, or dusted with mortar from the center will cause aggravated damage to the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T17:36:20-08:00","id":789509,"title":"","content":"Very interesting ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T18:04:02-08:00","id":789519,"title":"","content":"See the problem in second edition is that the pack gotta literally emulate the ban of the spirit, and those bans are quite stringent. Particularly because Uratha disregard toxicity per Primal Urge, so getting drunk? Or high? Is gonna get harder and harder.<br /> <br /> Booze is like toxicity 1, 2 at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T18:05:53-08:00","id":789520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/783037-totem-ban-and-bane-ideas-needeed?p=788875#post788875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bane: The spirit came into being in the abandoned apartment complex, feeding off of essence from the hosts of junkies and drug deals that passed hands there. The city managed to scrape up enough funds to knock down the building and erect a community rehab center focused on education about drug use. The bricks that make up the rehab's walls are the same bricks that cradled the spirit during it's formative time. <b>Weapons made from any brick</b>, or dusted with mortar from the center will cause aggravated damage to the spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool story; but you only craft weaponry for ease of use. Banes are simply substances that are detrimental to the spirit. So you could quite simply bash the spirit with the dislodged brick and fuck it up just the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T18:23:59-08:00","id":789531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/783037-totem-ban-and-bane-ideas-needeed?p=789520#post789520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool story; but you only craft weaponry for ease of use. Banes are simply substances that are detrimental to the spirit. So you could quite simply bash the spirit with the dislodged brick and fuck it up just the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but if you have a sense of style, you go with the weapon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T22:55:33-08:00","id":789620,"title":"","content":"Would the spirit be able to taint alcohol/drugs to increase their potency, allowing a werewolf to become intoxicated? That could be a good workaround.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T06:39:18-08:00","id":789701,"title":"","content":"Use of Stregnthten Influence: Drugs or Intoxication could do that, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}